/target
benchdata/
*.csv
!crates/**/testdata/*.csv
*.ferrix
*.ferrix-tmp/
*.fxedits
*.fxedits.tmp
# The other per-workbook sidecars (comments, formats, page setup, pivots,
# column sizing) and their autosaves/temps — user-local state, never source.
*.fxnotes
*.fxfmt
*.fxpage
*.fxpivot
*.fxsize
*.fx*.tmp
*.fxedits.autosave
# Agent-bridge command files (View → Agent bridge): local machine traffic.
*.fxagent
*.fxagent.out

# Agent-local helpers and handoff notes — never part of the source tree.
.ghenv.sh
REPORT.md

# Credential-bearing filenames (issue #60).
#
# Defense in depth, not the primary control: the primary control is not
# putting secrets in the working tree at all. This is the net that catches
# the mistake anyway — after the .ghenv.sh incident (an agent-committed
# token-sourcing helper, removed in #48), a `git add -A` from a tool or an
# agent is a realistic way for a key to reach a commit, and a committed
# secret is compromised the moment it is pushed, whether or not the commit
# is later reverted.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
# Public halves are not secret and are sometimes legitimately checked in
# (deploy keys, known-hosts fixtures), so they are exempted explicitly
# rather than caught by `id_rsa*` / `*.key` above.
!*.pub
